{#
  One form field — label, control, help text, required marker — wired the
  way 356 hand-written copies mostly weren't (design.md §7 companion).

  What the copies got wrong, counted: fourteen different label class
  combinations; 136 help texts of which exactly one was connected to its
  field with aria-describedby (a screen reader announced the label and
  nothing else — the format hint, the constraint, all invisible to the
  reader who needs them most); 96 required fields signalled by 19
  asterisks in one convention and nothing anywhere else. This partial
  renders the trio once, correctly: the help text carries
  `id="{field_id}-help"`, the control points at it, and `required` both
  sets the attribute and shows the one marker.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
      field_id: 'asset-name',
      field_name: 'name',          -- optional: a field a script reads by
                                   -- id and posts itself has no name
      label: 'Nom du bien',
      type: 'text',                -- text|email|url|tel|number|date|time|
                                   -- password|textarea|select (default text)
      value: asset.name,           -- optional
      help: 'Affiché publiquement.', -- optional, ARIA-wired
      required: true,              -- default false
      placeholder: '…',            -- optional
      maxlength: 100,              -- optional
      min: 0, max: 20, step: 1,    -- optional (number)
      inputmode: 'decimal',        -- optional
      rows: 4,                     -- textarea only
      options: [                   -- select only
          { value: 'a', label: 'A', selected: true, disabled: false,
            data: { 'first-import': '1' } },   -- optional data-* per option
      ],
      autocomplete: 'name',        -- optional
      size: 'sm',                  -- optional: the site's ONE compact
                                   -- variant (form-label small +
                                   -- form-control-sm/form-select-sm)
      disabled: true,              -- optional
      readonly: true,              -- optional
      pattern: '[0-9]{4}',         -- optional
      autofocus: true,             -- optional
      list: 'suggestions',         -- optional, id of a <datalist>
      describedby_extra: 'x-error',-- optional, id of an error/hint node
                                   -- rendered OUTSIDE this partial
      wrapper_class: 'mb-0',       -- optional, replaces the default mb-3
      control_class_extra: 'w-auto',-- optional, extra classes ON the control
      label_visually_hidden: true, -- optional: the row itself names the field
      data: { id: 4, url: '/x' },  -- optional data-* ON THE CONTROL
      aria_label: 'Vu par — Meute',-- optional, see below
  } only %}

  On `size`: the survey that preceded this partial's second pass found 34
  templates it could not serve, all for the same reason — their labels
  carried `small`, `fw-semibold`, `mb-1` or a combination, and their
  controls `form-control-sm`. Fourteen label variants is the disease, but
  "one size only" was too tight a cure: a dense settings table legitimately
  wants a compact field. So there are exactly two sizes, and `sm` is the
  only compact one. Anything reaching for a third belongs in design.md
  first.

  On `field_name`: omit it for a control that is never submitted with its
  form — a JS-driven settings panel reads its fields by id and builds the
  request itself, and a stray `name` on such a control only invites a
  future GET to carry it.

  On `data`: the control carries whatever the caller puts there, as
  `data-{key}`. Half the site's fields are read by a script that grips
  them through a `data-id` or a `data-endpoint`, and a partial that
  could not emit those simply excluded every one of them. The KEY is the
  attribute name after `data-` — `{ 'first-import': 1 }` renders
  `data-first-import="1"` — and the value is escaped like any other.

  On `label_visually_hidden`: a repeated row (one select per function, per
  album, per member) is named by the row, not by a label above each
  control — but a control with NO label is unreachable by name for a
  screen reader. The label is rendered and hidden, never dropped, and it
  must still say WHICH row it belongs to (« Rôle pour ANIM01 », not
  « Rôle »).

  On `aria_label`: the same problem when the label IS visible and has to
  stay short. A dozen calendars down a page each carrying a « Vu par »
  select gives a screen-reader user a dozen identically-named controls;
  the row names them on screen and nowhere else. This overrides the
  accessible name — so it MUST start with the visible label's own words
  (« Vu par — Meute », never « Visibilité du calendrier Meute »), or a
  visitor driving the page by voice asks for the control they can read
  and nothing answers (WCAG 2.5.3, Label in Name). Reach for
  `label_visually_hidden` first; this is for the case where the short
  label has to be on screen too.

  On `control_class_extra`: layout classes the caller owns — `w-auto` for
  a control inside a flex row, a hook class a script grips. Never a
  `form-control-sm`: that is `size`'s job, and putting it here would
  reintroduce the fourteen variants this partial exists to end.

  On `wrapper_class`: `mb-3` is the default and the right answer almost
  everywhere. A field inside a grid column or a single-row filter bar
  that supplies its own spacing passes its own class (often `mb-0`)
  rather than fight the margin with a second one.

  Passwords keep their own partial (password_field.html.twig — checklist,
  confirmation); rich text keeps rich_text_form_field.html.twig. This one
  is for everything simpler, which is most of the site.
#}
{% set _type = type|default('text') %}
{% set _required = required|default(false) %}
{% set _small = size|default('') == 'sm' %}
{% set _help_id = field_id ~ '-help' %}
{% set _described = [help|default('') ? _help_id : null, describedby_extra|default(null)]|filter(v => v)|join(' ') %}
{% set _control_class = (_type == 'select' ? 'form-select' : 'form-control')
    ~ (_small ? (_type == 'select' ? ' form-select-sm' : ' form-control-sm') : '')
    ~ (control_class_extra|default('') ? ' ' ~ control_class_extra : '') %}
{% set _wrapper = wrapper_class is defined ? wrapper_class : 'mb-3' %}
<div{% if _wrapper %} class="{{ _wrapper }}"{% endif %}>
    <label class="{{ label_visually_hidden|default(false) ? 'visually-hidden' : 'form-label' ~ (_small ? ' small' : '') }}" for="{{ field_id }}">
        {{- label -}}
        {%- if _required %} <span class="text-danger" aria-hidden="true">*</span>{% endif -%}
    </label>
    {% if _type == 'textarea' %}
        <textarea class="{{ _control_class }}" id="{{ field_id }}"
                  {%- if field_name is defined and field_name %} name="{{ field_name }}"{% endif %}
                  rows="{{ rows|default(4) }}"
                  {%- if _required %} required{% endif %}
                  {%- if disabled|default(false) %} disabled{% endif %}
                  {%- if readonly|default(false) %} readonly{% endif %}
                  {%- if autofocus|default(false) %} autofocus{% endif %}
                  {%- if maxlength|default(0) %} maxlength="{{ maxlength }}"{% endif %}
                  {%- if placeholder|default('') %} placeholder="{{ placeholder }}"{% endif %}
                  {%- if _described %} aria-describedby="{{ _described }}"{% endif %}
                  {%- if aria_label|default('') %} aria-label="{{ aria_label }}"{% endif %}
                  {%- for key, dval in data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ dval }}"{% endfor %}>{{ value|default('') }}</textarea>
    {% elseif _type == 'select' %}
        <select class="{{ _control_class }}" id="{{ field_id }}"
                {%- if field_name is defined and field_name %} name="{{ field_name }}"{% endif %}
                {%- if _required %} required{% endif %}
                {%- if disabled|default(false) %} disabled{% endif %}
                {%- if autofocus|default(false) %} autofocus{% endif %}
                {%- if _described %} aria-describedby="{{ _described }}"{% endif %}
                {%- if aria_label|default('') %} aria-label="{{ aria_label }}"{% endif %}
                {%- for key, dval in data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ dval }}"{% endfor %}>
            {% for option in options|default([]) %}
                <option value="{{ option.value }}"
                        {{- option.selected|default(false) ? ' selected' : '' }}
                        {{- option.disabled|default(false) ? ' disabled' : '' }}
                        {%- for key, dval in option.data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ dval }}"{% endfor %}>{{ option.label }}</option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
    {% else %}
        <input type="{{ _type }}" class="{{ _control_class }}" id="{{ field_id }}"
               {%- if field_name is defined and field_name %} name="{{ field_name }}"{% endif %}
               value="{{ value|default('') }}"
               {%- if _required %} required{% endif %}
               {%- if disabled|default(false) %} disabled{% endif %}
               {%- if readonly|default(false) %} readonly{% endif %}
               {%- if autofocus|default(false) %} autofocus{% endif %}
               {%- if maxlength|default(0) %} maxlength="{{ maxlength }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if min is defined %} min="{{ min }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if max is defined %} max="{{ max }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if step is defined %} step="{{ step }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if pattern|default('') %} pattern="{{ pattern }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if list|default('') %} list="{{ list }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if inputmode|default('') %} inputmode="{{ inputmode }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if placeholder|default('') %} placeholder="{{ placeholder }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if autocomplete|default('') %} autocomplete="{{ autocomplete }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if _described %} aria-describedby="{{ _described }}"{% endif %}
               {%- if aria_label|default('') %} aria-label="{{ aria_label }}"{% endif %}
               {%- for key, dval in data|default({}) %} data-{{ key }}="{{ dval }}"{% endfor %}>
    {% endif %}
    {% if help|default('') %}
        <div class="form-text" id="{{ _help_id }}">{{ help }}</div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
